        "original_id": "c18a2b9a-95f2-57b5-8c1b-b1d7ff2a8a67",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: \"What's It Gonna Be\", \"Love Shy (Thinking About You)\"\n- People: Selim Ben Rabha, Simon McDevitt, Aaron Evers, Mina Poli, Michelle McKenna\n- Groups: H \"Two\" O, Platnum\n- Concepts: bassline, UK garage\n- Places: Sheffield\n\nFacts:\n- Bassline, also called bassline house, Niche, or 4x4, is a music genre related to UK garage that originated in Sheffield in the early 2000s.\n- \"What's It Gonna Be\" is a bassline song performed by H \"Two\" O and the British three-person bassline vocal group Platnum.\n- H \"Two\" O is the duo of Selim Ben Rabha (\"Solution\") and Simon McDevitt (\"Oz\"), who also go by \"Hit 'Em\" and \"Hard.\"\n- Platnum consists of Aaron Evers, Mina Poli, and Michelle McKenna.\n- \"Love Shy (Thinking About You)\" was released after the success of \"What's It Gonna Be\" with H \"Two\" O.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
